  "articleBody": "Getting excited about a garage renovation is easy, but it’s just as easy to stumble into some common mistakes if you’re not careful. One of the biggest blunders we see is starting a project without a super clear plan. You've got to know what you want to use the space for, what your budget is, and what the timeline looks like. Don't skip that planning phase! Another common issue is underestimating the budget. Things can add up quickly, especially if you find unexpected repairs once you start tearing things out. Always factor in a little wiggle room for the unforeseen. Then there’s the material choice – picking flooring or other materials that just aren't suited for a garage's tough conditions is a frequent miss. Garages see a lot of abuse, so durability is key. Lastly, many folks bite off more than they can chew with DIY. If the project involves complex electrical, structural changes, or custom built-ins, trying to do it all yourself without the right skills or tools can lead to bigger problems (and more cost) down the road. For those trickier parts, or even just to get a solid plan in place, reaching out to a pro like HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of headaches.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
